# Review documents were un-ignored on the argument that they are the written
# record of why the code looks the way it does. That was reversed on 2026-08-01
# at the owner's instruction: reviews are working notes, not shipped artefacts,
# and they are excluded again by the `docs/*` and `*.md` rules above.
#
# NOTE for whoever reads this next: .gitignore has no effect on files git is
# ALREADY tracking. Fifteen review documents were tracked when this changed;
# removing them from the index is a separate, deliberate `git rm --cached` and
# is NOT done by this file. Check `git ls-files docs/reviews` before assuming.
#
# Roughly thirty source files and five test files cite `docs/reviews/*.md` by
# path in their comments. Those citations are prose only — no test resolves
# them on disk, so the suite stays green — but in a fresh clone they will point
# at files that are not there.
# !docs/reviews/*.md
# !docs/ai-guidance/reviews/*.md

